guide_gaps:
8.4 item 11, S4 (9.4), 12.5-12.6: a value-correct PHI crossing is invisible to trace events and to differential suites; only an IR read sees it, and the guide has no recipe for one. Fix: add a recipe to 12.5:
- traceinfo(tr).nins;
- traceir: ot>>8 via vmdef.irnames, ot&0x40 for PHI, ot&0x80 for guard, op2&0x3ff for a CONV's mode;
- operands are bias-relative (instructions positive, constants negative, and tracek takes the negative ones). [F, R]

8.2 steps 0 and 6:
- a pristine file is `git cat-file blob <pin>:src/<f>` (LF); build/native has no export directory;
- "oclj_bitwidth( on N lines" counts comments too;
- moving an include changes NADD;
- two changes to one script merge with additive NADD (45+18+8=71), and git merge-file on the test files leaves predictable conflicts in the part lists.
Fix: add these to steps 0 and 6. [F, C]

11.3, 12.4:
- under -Omaxside=0 a hot exit still gets a "fallback to interpreter" stub;
- a patched exit fires no texit event;
- a speculative guard also needs -Ohotexit=1, -Otryside=1 -Ohotexit=2, -Omaxside=1 and -Ohotloop=1 -Omaxside=0;
- an index fold also needs -O-abc, -O-narrow, -O-fuse, -O-fwd -O-dse and -O-sink.
Fix: add those option sets and the exit-count caveat. [R, VR, VF]

